原因非常简单。

678
00:58:23,360 --> 00:58:28,230
We created CPUs for humans in the past.
过去我们为人类设计 CPU。

679
00:58:28,280 --> 00:58:32,030
And humans, they're only 1 billion of us.
而人类只有约 10 亿人。

680
00:58:32,080 --> 00:58:35,430
There will be billions of agents.
未来将有数十亿智能体。

681
00:58:35,480 --> 00:58:45,030
And these agents are going to be using the CPUs with very little patience because the cost of the GPU they sit next to is too high.
这些智能体对 CPU 的使用将极为急切，因为它们旁边 GPU 的成本过高。

682
00:58:45,080 --> 00:58:49,510
And therefore too valuable, too precious.
因此，这些 CPU 也过于宝贵、过于珍贵。

683
00:58:49,560 --> 00:58:59,150
Therefore, these CPUs are going to be both performant but they also have to be extremely energy efficient.
所以这些 CPU 必须兼具高性能和极高的能效。

684
00:58:59,200 --> 00:59:10,870
So that we can cram as much CPUs we can into the factory without taking away power from the token generation, which we know is how we make money.
这样我们才能在不占用词元生成电力的前提下，尽可能多地塞入 CPU，而词元生成正是我们赚钱的方式。

685
00:59:10,920 --> 00:59:12,273
These four properties,
这四个特性，

686
00:59:12,323 --> 00:59:19,790
instructions per clock or single-threaded performance bandwidth per core the total bandwidth
每时钟周期指令数或单线程性能、每核带宽以及芯片内外的总带宽

687
00:59:19,840 --> 00:59:25,545
around the chip and inside the chip and energy efficiency defines Vera.
和能效共同定义了 Vera。

688
00:59:25,595 --> 00:59:27,738
It is absolutely world class.
它绝对属于世界级水平。

689
00:59:27,788 --> 00:59:33,510
When you compare it to the highest performance x86, it is just off the charts.
与最高性能的 x86 处理器相比，它的表现简直超乎想象。

690
00:59:33,560 --> 00:59:42,630
When you compare it in real single-threaded performance, real performance, it's off the charts.
在实际单线程性能上进行对比，它的表现同样超乎想象。

691
00:59:42,680 --> 00:59:46,991
It is incredible to be able to deliver 5% improvement on CPUs.
能够在 CPU 上实现 5% 的性能提升，已经令人难以置信。

